          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Body mass index (BMI) relates an adult’s mass to their height.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p6-q6-formula",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The formula for BMI is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "b=\\frac{m}{h^2}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " where ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "m",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is mass in kilograms and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "h",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is height in metres.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Mr Ding has a mass of 68 kg and height of 181 cm. Calculate his BMI. Round your answer to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$b=20.76$",
          "worked": "$181\\text{ cm}=1.81\\text{ m}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}b &= \\frac{m}{h^2} \\\\ b &= \\frac{68}{(1.81)^2} \\\\ b &= \\frac{68}{3.2761} \\\\ b &\\approx 20.76\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Someone found Mr Ding’s BMI to be $0.0020756\\ldots$ What mistake have they made?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "They used height in centimetres instead of metres.",
          "worked": "They substituted $h=181$ instead of $h=1.81$:\n$$\\begin{align*}b &= \\frac{68}{181^2} \\\\ b &\\approx 0.0020756\\end{align*}$$\nThe formula requires height in metres.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "For this question, use the target range $21<b<25$. Based on Mr Ding’s BMI, what change in his mass would bring his BMI into this range, assuming his height stays the same?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "His mass would need to increase slightly, since his BMI is below 21.",
          "worked": "His BMI is approximately $20.76$, which is below $21$. With height unchanged, increasing mass increases $b=\\frac{m}{h^2}$. His mass would therefore need to increase slightly to bring his BMI into the stated range.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      }
    ]
  },
